	ida_struct.set_member_cmt(ida_struct.get_member(struc, 204928), '''String: "TERMS OF USE AND COMMUNITY DATA POLICY\n\nWelcome to the Smart Dashcam feature.\n\nWe built this feature not only to help you capture beautiful moments on the road or keep evidence to protect your rights in case of an accident, but with a bigger ambition: Together, let\'s create a vibrant, accurate, and safe traffic map for everyone.\n\nBelow are important terms about how we handle data to achieve that goal.\n\nI. TRAFFIC DATA CONTRIBUTION PROGRAM\nTo keep the map system updated with the latest changes (such as new traffic signs, speed limit changes, or road construction), we need the cooperation of our user community.\n\n1. How it works\nThe system will extract still frames (images) from your dashcam videos for analysis by artificial intelligence (AI).\n\nSole purpose: To recognize traffic signs, road markings, traffic conditions, and road status.\n\nPrivacy protection (Anonymization): We commit to anonymizing all extracted images. We care about \"traffic signs,\" not your identity or that of bystanders.\n\n2. For Free Users\nTo maintain high-quality free service and free server hosting for the community:\n\nMandatory participation: By using the free version, you agree to join the \"Traffic Community\" program.\n\nContribution: The app will automatically extract and send anonymized image data to our system to improve the map. This is your valuable contribution to \"pay\" with data, helping the driving community stay safer.\n\n3. For Premium Users\nAs a premium user, you have greater control, but we still hope for your support:\n\nOpt-out option: You have the right to TURN OFF image data contribution in Settings > \"Utilities\" > \"Dashcam\" at any time.\n\nA call from the development team: Although you can turn it off, we encourage you to keep this feature ON. Data from Premium users is often of higher quality and stability, playing a key role in making speed alerts more accurate for you and the community.\n\nAnonymization mechanism: Even if you enable this feature, image data is still processed anonymously. We do not track your private routes through images.\n\nII. LEGAL DISCLAIMER\nTo ensure a safe and lawful environment, please note the following:\n\n1. Safety first\nDo not operate while driving: The app is designed to work automatically. You must not adjust settings, review videos, or modify the app while the vehicle is moving.\n\nDriver responsibility: The app is only a support tool. You are fully responsible for safe vehicle operation and compliance with local traffic laws. We are not liable for any accidents, injuries, or property damage occurring while you use the app.\n\n2. User-Generated Content\nPrivacy of others: You are legally responsible for the video content you record. Do not use the app to unlawfully invade others\' privacy or record in restricted areas (military zones, national security areas).\n\nOwnership: You retain ownership of the original videos stored on your device.\n\n3. Accuracy of alert data\nReference only: Information about speed limits, signs, or traffic conditions provided by the app is aggregated from algorithms and the community. While we strive for the highest accuracy, this data is for reference only.\n\nReal-world priority: Actual road signs and orders always have the highest legal value and override any information in the app. We disclaim responsibility for any traffic violations or fines incurred by users based on app information."''', True)
	ida_struct.set_member_cmt(ida_struct.get_member(struc, 204920), '''String: "Dashcam Terms of Service"''', True)
